Worst cell: B0006 with MAE 6.76.
It degrades to 56.7% SOH but the model only ever predicts down to 69.6%.
A tree ensemble trained on cells that never fade this hard
extrapolates by averaging toward the training floor, so
severe degradation is systematically under-predicted.
This is a data-coverage limit, not a tuning problem: no
hyperparameter setting can invent a degradation the
training cells never exhibited.


